// 🔴 The sheet's own `variant` field is `Transform`, but this does NOT use
// `CharacterAbility::Transform` (`common/src/comp/ability.rs`). Investigated
// that variant in full first:
//
// - `common/src/states/transform.rs` + `server/src/events/entity_manipulation.rs`
//   `transform_entity()`: on activation it emits `TransformEvent`, which
//   overwrites the target's real `Inventory`, `Stats`, `SkillSet`, `Poise`,
//   `Health`, `Energy`, `Body`, `Mass`, `Density`, `Collider` and active
//   abilities with an entirely different `EntityConfig`'s values, and
//   explicitly disables persistence while doing so (`'persist: { ... }` block).
// - `allow_players` is documented on the variant itself: "Only set to `true`
//   for admin only abilities since this disables persistence and is not
//   intended to be used by regular players." Its only two shipped call sites
//   (`custom/cursekeeper/transform.ron`, `debug/evolve.ron`) both set it
//   `false`/admin-triggered, and there is no revert-after-duration mechanism
//   anywhere in the state (`transform.rs` has no timer that transforms the
//   entity back) — it is a one-way NPC-swap primitive built for boss/debug
//   triggers, not a reversible ~60s player self-buff.
// Using it here would wipe the caster's real gear/stats for the spell's
// duration with no automatic way back — unacceptable for a temporary player
// buff, and would require new Rust (a revert-on-expiry mechanism) to fix.
//
// The correct existing primitive instead: `BuffKind::Polymorphed`
// (`common/src/comp/buff.rs`) + `BuffEffect::BodyChange`
// (`common/systems/src/buff.rs` line ~811: `body_override.unwrap_or(stat.
// original_body)` — the body is automatically reconciled back to
// `stat.original_body` the instant the buff is no longer active, giving a
// real, already-*shipped*-for-players auto-revert with zero extra Rust).
// Already used by a real player-facing drinkable, `potion_curious.ron`
// ("Curious Potion"), which grants exactly this buff with a
// `MiscBuffData::Body(...)` payload and a timed duration. This is the
// buff-based polymorph machinery that is already proven safe for players —
// unlike the literal `Transform` variant, which stays untouched by any
// player spell.
//
// Kept branch: the sheet's third option, "wearing an altered appearance" —
// `Polymorphed` can only swap to one *fixed*, fully-specified `Body` value
// (no per-cast "choose claws vs. gills vs. a new face" choice exists in the
// data model), so this authors one concrete alternate form rather than the
// sheet's three player-chosen options. `FishMedium(Marlin)` mirrors
// `potion_curious.ron`'s exact same-primitive usage (a small/medium
// creature swap) most closely, of the school's few simple-struct `Body`
// variants (`Humanoid::Body` needs 8 additional cosmetic fields with no
// serde default, `FishMedium`/`FishSmall`/`QuadrupedLow` need only
// `species`+`body_type`).
// Dropped: "growing natural weapons" (damage_type: Bludgeoning) — no
// `BuffEffect` grants an attack-damage bonus tied to `Polymorphed`, and
// "adopting aquatic traits" as a *swim-speed* buff specifically — the only
// swim-speed-granting kind, `BuffKind::SalamanderAspect`, is commented out
// in the enum (`// SalamanderAspect, TODO: Readd in second dwarven mine MR`,
// `common/src/comp/buff.rs`), not a live variant today.
SelfBuff(
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    cast_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    buffs: [
        BuffDesc(
            kind: Polymorphed,
            data: BuffData(
                strength: 0.0,
                duration: Some(60.0),
                misc_data: Some(Body(FishMedium((species: Marlin, body_type: Male)))),
            ),
        ),
    ],
    energy_cost: 40,
    enforced_limit: true,
    meta: (
        school: Some(Transmutation),
        source: Some(Arcane),
        // level 2 spell -> min_level 12, same `level * 6` convention.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(12)),
    ),
)
